R-AD35 R-AP1 R-AP52 R-AP34 R-E6 R-IX7 R-RG4 R-EC15 (slice 206f): the first R-AP1 read of `tln add` with a registry gets an answer that Talon cannot use: run 1 a 502 `/errors/upstream`, run 2 a 429 `/errors/rate-limited` with `Retry-After: 30`, run 3 a 302. Each run is exit 15 with the text of the registry error (the same code as every registry read, slice 202). No retry (R-AP34), no GitHub list, no ingest (R-AD35 starts at a 404), no closure query, no write of the project. Each run has its own repository, so the kept public answer of a run does not change the next.
Run 1 is a first run on p1 (projects.json and path-roc.json are written, the fake tty is read). Runs 2 and 3 have the later prefix (the pattern of registry/al2-install-query run 2).
